course: dictionary
lesson: 8472
title: Salty: taste, sea and slang
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Salty most often means tasting of salt, or having salt in it. «Most of Earth's water is salty water in the oceans; only a small part is fresh.» The clue is the word water: the oceans are salty, but rivers and lakes are not.
explain: Context also shows you which meaning is right. «The salty sea air» is in a story about the seaside, so salty means the air tastes and smells of the sea. In a science sentence, salty describes water you could measure, not a feeling.
explain: Salty can also be informal slang. In this lesson, «salty» = cross, so a salty reply is a rude or cross reply. Check by swapping in your meaning: a cross reply makes sense, but a reply that tastes of salt does not.
fact: Salty means tasting of salt or having salt in it.
fact: Salty water has salt dissolved in it, and most of Earth's water is salty water in the oceans.
fact: Salty water freezes at a lower temperature than plain water, which is why salt is spread on icy roads.
fact: Informal slang: «salty» can mean a bit rude or cross, as in «a salty reply».
fact: The Baltic Sea is brackish: «much less salty than the ocean», because fresh river water pours into it.
exercise: «The salty sea air made the children hungry.» What does salty mean here? | Very cross | Very cold | Full of sand | *Tasting of salt, from the sea
exercise: «Wow, that reply was salty!» What does salty mean in this slang? | Sleepy | Wet and sticky | *A bit rude or cross | Hot and spicy
exercise: The Baltic Sea is brackish, much less salty than the ocean. What does «less salty» mean? | Deeper | Louder | Colder | *Contains less salt
test: «Salt is spread on icy roads because salty water freezes at a lower temperature.» What is salty water? | *Water with salt dissolved in it | Water from a tap only | Water that is boiling hot | Water that is fizzy
test: Mum says, «Don't be so salty about it!» What does she mean? | *Don't be so cross | Don't go near the sea | Don't taste it | Don't add more salt
exam: Ella says salty only ever means seawater. Which explanation is best? | *Salty means tasting of salt, and in slang it can mean cross | Salty always means cross | Salty is a kind of sea animal | Salty means only sea creatures
